with `playAmbientSound` now featuring a sound name property and description. I\'ve also defined a `saveNote` function call for storing session mentions. Finally, I\'m working on a `getSystemInfo` call to retrieve context.\n\n\n**Implementing Session Connections**\n\nI\'m now focusing on handling client WebSocket connections to `/live`, including parsing query parameters like `voiceName` and `userName`. I am setting up the Gemini Live session, specifying the model, audio modality, and custom voice name via `prebuiltVoiceConfig`. I\'m also incorporating system instructions and tools configuration and preparing the data I need to send to the client. I am working on the audio callbacks and data extraction.\n\n\n**Managing WebSocket Message Types**\n\nI am now structuring message handling within the WebSocket server, specifically `/live`. I\'m focusing on sending appropriately typed JSON messages back to the client. I\'ve implemented logic to send `interrupted`, `turnComplete`, `transcript` (for both user and Navi), and `toolCall` messages, using message.serverContent and message.toolCall data.\n\n\n**Handling Gemini Live Session**\n\nI\'m now implementing the Gemini Live session event handlers. Specifically, I\'m defining `onmessage`, `onclose`, and `onerror` to manage client communication and error handling. I am also working on parsing incoming client messages of different types. I am making sure to format the outbound messages as appropriately-typed JSON objects. I am testing it too!\n\n\n"
