steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1785256127
      nanos: 724349057
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "# Feature: Integrated Browser for Navi\n\nImplement a fully integrated browser inside the Navi desktop application using Electron.\n\n## Objective\n\nThe browser should be built directly into the application so users never need to switch to Google Chrome. Navi should be able to navigate websites, open tabs, and interact with web pages through voice commands and tool calling.\n\nThe experience should feel like a modern AI operating system rather than a browser.\n\n---\n\n## Technology\n\n- Electron\n- React\n- TypeScript\n- Vite\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Electron BrowserView or WebContentsView\n- IPC communication between Renderer and Main process\n\n---\n\n## Browser Layout\n\nThe application should use a split layout.\n\nLeft Section:\n- Navi voice assistant\n- Animated AI orb\n- Waveform\n- Connection status\n- Voice controls\n\nRight Section:\n- Embedded Chromium browser\n\nThe browser should occupy approximately 70% of the window.\n\nNavi panel should occupy approximately 30%.\n\nAllow resizing by dragging the divider.\n\n---\n\n## Browser Features\n\nImplement:\n\n- Multiple tabs\n- Address bar\n- Back\n- Forward\n- Refresh\n- Home\n- Bookmark support\n- Downloads\n- Loading progress\n- New tab\n- Close tab\n- Duplicate tab\n\n---\n\n## AI Integration\n\nNavi can control the browser using voice.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Open YouTube\"\n\n\"Search for React tutorials\"\n\n\"Open Gmail\"\n\n\"Go back\"\n\n\"Refresh this page\"\n\n\"Open GitHub\"\n\n\"Scroll down\"\n\n\"Scroll to the top\"\n\n\"Zoom in\"\n\n\"Open a new tab\"\n\n\"Close this tab\"\n\n\"Switch to the second tab\"\n\n---\n\n## Browser Tool API\n\nCreate browser tools.\n\nnavigate(url)\n\nsearchGoogle(query)\n\ngoBack()\n\ngoForward()\n\nreload()\n\nnewTab(url)\n\ncloseTab(id)\n\nswitchTab(id)\n\nscrollUp()\n\nscrollDown()\n\nscrollToTop()\n\nscrollToBottom()\n\nzoomIn()\n\nzoomOut()\n\nfindOnPage(text)\n\ncopyCurrentUrl()\n\ndownloadFile(url)\n\nprintPage()\n\ngetCurrentPageTitle()\n\ngetCurrentUrl()\n\n---\n\n## Browser Events\n\nEmit events when:\n\nPage starts loading\n\nPage finishes loading\n\nNavigation changes\n\nTitle changes\n\nURL changes\n\nDownloads begin\n\nDownloads finish\n\nNew tab opens\n\nTab closes\n\n---\n\n## Browser Memory\n\nNavi should remember during the active session:\n\nRecently opened websites\n\nFrequently visited sites\n\nCurrent active tab\n\nCurrent page title\n\nLast search query\n\n---\n\n## Browser Voice Feedback\n\nExamples:\n\n\"I\'ve opened YouTube.\"\n\n\"Searching for React tutorials.\"\n\n\"This page is still loading.\"\n\n\"I switched to your GitHub tab.\"\n\n\"I found three matches on this page.\"\n\n\"Download completed.\"\n\n---\n\n## UI\n\nUse a premium glassmorphism theme.\n\nBrowser toolbar should match the rest of Navi.\n\nRounded corners\n\nSoft shadows\n\nBlurred background\n\nAnimated transitions\n\nDark mode\n\nPurple/Blue accent colors\n\n---\n\n## Performance\n\nTabs should remain alive in the background.\n\nFast tab switching.\n\nLazy load inactive tabs.\n\nPreserve session after restart.\n\nMinimize memory usage.\n\n---\n\n## Security\n\nDisable Node integration inside browser pages.\n\nEnable Context Isolation.\n\nUse secure preload scripts.\n\nValidate all IPC communication.\n\nSandbox browser content.\n\nPrevent arbitrary code execution.\n\n---\n\n## Future Compatibility\n\nDesign the browser so future features can be added without major refactoring.\n\nFuture modules include:\n\nDeveloper tools\n\nAI page summarization\n\nAI webpage explanation\n\nScreenshot analysis\n\nPDF reader\n\nBrowser history search\n\nPassword manager integration\n\nVoice form filling\n\nVoice shopping assistant\n\nWeb automation\n\nSplit screen browsing\n\nPinned tabs\n\nWorkspace sessions\n\nCloud sync\n\nThe browser architecture should be modular, scalable, and suitable for future AI-powered capabilities."
    items {
      text: "# Feature: Integrated Browser for Navi\n\nImplement a fully integrated browser inside the Navi desktop application using Electron.\n\n## Objective\n\nThe browser should be built directly into the application so users never need to switch to Google Chrome. Navi should be able to navigate websites, open tabs, and interact with web pages through voice commands and tool calling.\n\nThe experience should feel like a modern AI operating system rather than a browser.\n\n---\n\n## Technology\n\n- Electron\n- React\n- TypeScript\n- Vite\n- Tailwind CSS\n- Electron BrowserView or WebContentsView\n- IPC communication between Renderer and Main process\n\n---\n\n## Browser Layout\n\nThe application should use a split layout.\n\nLeft Section:\n- Navi voice assistant\n- Animated AI orb\n- Waveform\n- Connection status\n- Voice controls\n\nRight Section:\n- Embedded Chromium browser\n\nThe browser should occupy approximately 70% of the window.\n\nNavi panel should occupy approximately 30%.\n\nAllow resizing by dragging the divider.\n\n---\n\n## Browser Features\n\nImplement:\n\n- Multiple tabs\n- Address bar\n- Back\n- Forward\n- Refresh\n- Home\n- Bookmark support\n- Downloads\n- Loading progress\n- New tab\n- Close tab\n- Duplicate tab\n\n---\n\n## AI Integration\n\nNavi can control the browser using voice.\n\nExamples:\n\n\"Open YouTube\"\n\n\"Search for React tutorials\"\n\n\"Open Gmail\"\n\n\"Go back\"\n\n\"Refresh this page\"\n\n\"Open GitHub\"\n\n\"Scroll down\"\n\n\"Scroll to the top\"\n\n\"Zoom in\"\n\n\"Open a new tab\"\n\n\"Close this tab\"\n\n\"Switch to the second tab\"\n\n---\n\n## Browser Tool API\n\nCreate browser tools.\n\nnavigate(url)\n\nsearchGoogle(query)\n\ngoBack()\n\ngoForward()\n\nreload()\n\nnewTab(url)\n\ncloseTab(id)\n\nswitchTab(id)\n\nscrollUp()\n\nscrollDown()\n\nscrollToTop()\n\nscrollToBottom()\n\nzoomIn()\n\nzoomOut()\n\nfindOnPage(text)\n\ncopyCurrentUrl()\n\ndownloadFile(url)\n\nprintPage()\n\ngetCurrentPageTitle()\n\ngetCurrentUrl()\n\n---\n\n## Browser Events\n\nEmit events when:\n\nPage starts loading\n\nPage finishes loading\n\nNavigation changes\n\nTitle changes\n\nURL changes\n\nDownloads begin\n\nDownloads finish\n\nNew tab opens\n\nTab closes\n\n---\n\n## Browser Memory\n\nNavi should remember during the active session:\n\nRecently opened websites\n\nFrequently visited sites\n\nCurrent active tab\n\nCurrent page title\n\nLast search query\n\n---\n\n## Browser Voice Feedback\n\nExamples:\n\n\"I\'ve opened YouTube.\"\n\n\"Searching for React tutorials.\"\n\n\"This page is still loading.\"\n\n\"I switched to your GitHub tab.\"\n\n\"I found three matches on this page.\"\n\n\"Download completed.\"\n\n---\n\n## UI\n\nUse a premium glassmorphism theme.\n\nBrowser toolbar should match the rest of Navi.\n\nRounded corners\n\nSoft shadows\n\nBlurred background\n\nAnimated transitions\n\nDark mode\n\nPurple/Blue accent colors\n\n---\n\n## Performance\n\nTabs should remain alive in the background.\n\nFast tab switching.\n\nLazy load inactive tabs.\n\nPreserve session after restart.\n\nMinimize memory usage.\n\n---\n\n## Security\n\nDisable Node integration inside browser pages.\n\nEnable Context Isolation.\n\nUse secure preload scripts.\n\nValidate all IPC communication.\n\nSandbox browser content.\n\nPrevent arbitrary code execution.\n\n---\n\n## Future Compatibility\n\nDesign the browser so future features can be added without major refactoring.\n\nFuture modules include:\n\nDeveloper tools\n\nAI page summarization\n\nAI webpage explanation\n\nScreenshot analysis\n\nPDF reader\n\nBrowser history search\n\nPassword manager integration\n\nVoice form filling\n\nVoice shopping assistant\n\nWeb automation\n\nSplit screen browsing\n\nPinned tabs\n\nWorkspace sessions\n\nCloud sync\n\nThe browser architecture should be modular, scalable, and suitable for future AI-powered capabilities."
    }
  }
}
