  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing the Prompt\'s Core**\n\nI\'m currently dissecting the prompt\'s request, focusing on the core components. I\'ve begun mapping the conceptual architecture of an \"Integrated Browser for Navi.\" The initial stage includes splitting the layout into distinct sections: a Navi voice assistant section and the main browser content area. I\'m prioritizing the features for each part.\n\n\n**Defining Browser Feature Set**\n\nI\'m now detailing the embedded browser\'s capabilities. It will be a fully-featured component with multiple tabs, a dynamic address bar, comprehensive navigation, downloads, and history management. I\'ve designed a sandboxed iframe/webview with zoom, scroll, find, copy URL, print, and AI-powered summarization. Also including a quick start dashboard with frequent bookmarks and a search bar for efficient navigation.\n\n\n**Integrating Voice Command Functions**\n\nI\'m now integrating AI voice control. I\'ve defined function declarations for `server.ts` and `ToolManager.ts`, linking the `ToolManager` to the browser controller state. I\'ve designed functions for navigation, Google search, history manipulation (back, forward, reload), tab management (new, close, switch), scrolling, zooming, and even URL copying.\n\n\n**Implementing Browser Tools**\n\nI\'m now detailing the voice interaction with the browser\'s functionalities. I\'ve designed function declarations for `Url()`, `getCurrentPageTitle()`, `getCurrentUrl()`, `findOnPage(text: string)`, and `summarizePage()`. These allow the user to easily copy the active tab\'s URL, return its title, find text, or summarize the content. I\'ve also planned voice feedback, a browser memory for history tracking, and a glassmorphism UI. Step one updates `server.ts` with system prompts and tool declarations for navigation, Google search, and `goBack`.\n\n\n**Expanding Browser Commands**\n\nI\'m now expanding the voice command suite. I\'ve integrated commands like `goForward`, `reload`, and `zoomOut`, enriching the core function set. I\'m also including `newTab`, `closeTab`, `switchTab`, and scrolling functionality such as `scrollUp`, `scrollDown`, `scrollToTop`, `scrollToBottom`, and utilities such as `copyCurrentUrl`, `getCurrentPageTitle`, and `getCurrentUrl`. I\'ve updated the `NAVI_SYSTEM_PROMPT` in `server.ts` to reflect the integrated nature of Navi as the AI Browser Assistant.\n\nI\'m now progressing to Step 2, focusing on the creation of a Browser State Manager and React components. I\'m defining crucial types within `/src/types/browser.ts`, including `TabItem`, `BookmarkItem`, `HistoryItem`, `DownloadItem`, and `BrowserState`. Then, I\'m building `/src/components/Browser/BrowserContainer.tsx`, which will encapsulate the full right panel of the browser and consist of a Tab Bar and a Navigation & Address Bar.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 41679593
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
