    modified_response: "I have updated **Navi AI OS** to directly control your installed Google Chrome application and rendered Navi as a small floating companion widget:\n\n- **Complete Embedded Browser Removal**: Deleted all internal browser container and drawer components (`BrowserContainer`, `NewTabDashboard`, `BookmarksDrawer`, `HistoryDrawer`, `DownloadsDrawer`, `PageSummaryModal`). No websites, iframes, or WebViews are rendered inside Navi.\n- **External Google Chrome Automation**: Updated `ToolManager` and server instructions so Navi controls your desktop Google Chrome app. When you say commands like *\"Play music\"*, *\"Open YouTube\"*, *\"Search Naruto\"*, or *\"Gmail\"*, Navi opens or activates the target site in your system Google Chrome window while reusing your existing Chrome session.\n- **Floating Companion Widget**: Created a small, draggable, always-on-top companion widget (`FloatingCompanionWidget.tsx`) occupying less than 20% of the viewport. It features:\n  - **Current Action Badge**: Displays Chrome activation status (e.g. *\"Google Chrome Activated \342\206\222 YouTube Music\"*).\n  - **Voice Waveform & Animated Orb**: Real-time visual feedback for listening and speaking states.\n  - **Listening / Speaking Indicators**: Dynamic status badges with pulsing animations.\n  - **Interactive Controls**: Dedicated Pause/Resume, Stop/Disconnect, Mute/Unmute Mic buttons, and current media title display.\n  - **Quick Utility Toolbar**: Direct access to voice selector, ambient audio player, notes drawer, and tool execution logs."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
